# Agent stack (Synthex — May 2026)

## Models (Cursor)

| Context | Model | Notes |
|---------|--------|--------|
| Interactive Agent / Composer | **Composer 2.5 Fast** | Default in picker after Cursor update (May 2026+) |
| Background agents, ship-loop, batch | **Composer 2.5 Standard** | Same intelligence, lower cost |
| Architecture / high-stakes | Opus or GPT per task | Not replaced by Composer 2.5 |

Changelog: https://cursor.com/changelog/composer-2-5

## Hooks (Indy Dev Dan contract)

- PreToolUse shell hook: `node .cursor/hooks/pre-bash-validate.cjs`
- Hook stdout must be **one JSON line only**: `{"permission":"allow"}` or `{"permission":"deny",...}`
- Never use bare `echo` in `.cmd` when stdin is piped
- Smoke test: `powershell -File scripts/test-cursor-prebash-hook.ps1`
- Troubleshooting: `.cursor/HOOKS-FIX.md`, skill `cursor-hooks-windows`

## Karpathy-inspired execution

1. State assumptions; ask if unclear — do not guess.
2. Simplest correct diff — no speculative features.
3. Surgical edits — only what the task requires.
4. Goal-driven verification — run commands, paste output before claiming done.

Banned: "should work", "probably passes", "seems correct".

## gstack (selective)

- Enabled globally: **`/qa`**, **`/cso`** only (explicit invocation).
- Do not auto-run other gstack commands — Synthex skill catalog covers CEO/design/ship.
- Do not run `./setup --team` in this repo.

## Codex CLI

- Keep `@openai/codex` updated (`npm i -g @openai/codex@latest`) for optional sidecar review.
- `codex-adversarial` is **manual only** on auth/payments/migrations — never in autonomous loops.

## CI merge policy

- **Blocking:** GitHub Actions (Build, tests, lint, security gates).
- **Ignorable unless branch protection requires it:** `Vercel – synthex-sandbox`.
- **Use for preview QA:** `Vercel – synthex` preview URL on the PR.

